# Draws a chain of segments with the Segment tool on the sketch example:
# from E, snapped and shared, to a new point P1 level with it within 2
# degrees (the H suggestion, kept); from P1, snapped, a segment whose length
# 0.5 is typed over the canvas and applied with Enter, its end P2 placed by
# a click; from P2, snapped, to P3; a fourth one started, then dropped by
# Esc. A second Esc quits the tool, and an undo takes back the third
# segment.
open docs/instances/sketch-basic.json
wait 16
action tool.segment
wait 2
click L 837 532
click L 515 523
click L 515 532
wait 2
text "0.5"
wait 2
key Enter
wait 2
click L 482 452
click L 484 458
click L 740 307
click L 788 371
key Escape
key Escape
wait 2
action edit.undo
wait 2
